{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses was tending the flock of Jethro.</b> The commentators said: since every shepherd is disqualified because he grazes animals in others' fields and is suspected of theft, therefore it stated that these sheep belonged to Jethro — and a man does not sin to his own loss. But in any case it was necessary to inform us that he was a shepherd, for most of the prophets attained prophecy through shepherding, since prophecy requires solitude, and through seeing the heavens, the work of the hands of Elohim — as it is written (Psalms 8:4), ״כִּי אֶרְאֶה שָׁמֶיךָ מַעֲשֵׂה אֶצְבְּעֹתֶיךָ״ and so forth — for through this all his thought will be fixed upon the existence of HaShem, blessed be He, until the spirit of YHWH is poured upon him from on high, something not found so readily in one who sits in his house or who does some other labor in the field, other than the shepherd, who sits free and unoccupied most of the time."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:17:58.262312066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}